  "summary": "Billionaire Chris Larsen, who has donated over $12 million to fund SFPD's Flock camera network and Real-Time Investigation Center, told Kara Swisher's podcast that San Francisco's one-year retention period for Flock data is too long and should be shortened. The article notes SFPD's Flock system was improperly searched nearly 300 times by federal and out-of-state agencies, and the city's Flock contract is up for renewal in February 2027.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "San Francisco keeps Flock information for a year. That's way more than the average. The average is about 30 days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "The SFPD disclosed in June that its Flock network had been improperly searched nearly 300 times on behalf of federal and out-of-state agencies over roughly a year, despite state law and department policy restricting access.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
